# rlxfw's release label.  One line; everything else is a comment.
#
# NOTHING READS THE VALUE.  It reaches the image only through RECIPE_ID, the
# sha256 over every file under config/ and kernel/ (tools/rlxfw-kbuild.sh), so
# two builds that differ in nothing but this line print different RLXFW-ID0
# lines at boot.  RLXFW-ID0 names the kernel recipe, not the image
# (docs/known-issues/v1.0.md): a userspace change alone does not move it, and
# this file is how a release candidate gets an identity of its own.
#
# P6r-10's bench round needs exactly that: U, version 7, is installed through
# httpd over V, version 6, and the boot after it is identified by RLXFW-ID0
# against U's build (notes/self-update.md § 6.1).  V was built before this file
# existed.  Change the label for each release candidate.
v1.1-rc1
